Coded. One row, chair **5**.

- **V1/V3:** three `record` passages on one instrument, HB2492 (2022) — the House Third Reading roll call (`CARROLL Y CARTER Y CHAPLIK Y`, `Passed 31-26-3-0-0`), the enacted Chapter 99 text, and the bill overview listing `Carter (Co-Sponsor)`. `actor_quote`/`tally_quote` sit on the pages that print them; `provision_quote` sits on the bill text only.
- **V2:** on-question — the bill's operative requirement is proof of citizenship at registration, which is exactly what the ladder's top rung names.
- **V4:** chair-shaped. Single-subject bill ("voter registration; verification; citizenship"); 26 No votes, so not near-unanimous. No photo-ID or mail-ballot ID-number clause, so the rung-3/rung-4 readings are excluded by the bill's own text.
- **V5:** in-term — the 2022 act falls inside his 2021-11-05 to 2023-01-09 House term, same chamber and office.
- No candidate quotes: every source is statutory or procedural text, not his words. `needs_source` empty.
